Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.869 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  there's a primal urge in all of us to  explore  in the closing shot of for all mankind's  second season we got our first glimpse  of 1995  and a human walking on the surface of  mars in the first trailer for season  three there's a whole lot of mars action  with a three-way race to get there first  hey guys pete here today i'm going to  break down that season 3 trailer which  looks pretty amazing as is the show's  custom we will be moving forward in time  we left things in 1983 after danny and  stephen decided to go through with  apollo soyuz and ed decided to take down  sea dragon himself it looks like the  mars landing will happen in 1995 but the  season picks up in 1992  giving us time to see how that race  develops the trailer opens with dany  saying that there's a primal urge in all  of us to explore we see a shot of her on  the u.s mission coupled with a shot of  ed and civilian clothes on what looks  like this large ship that has a rotating  wheel to create artificial gravity this  is also known as a von braun wheel  because werner who you'll remember from  season one used this idea as part of a  concept ship he came up with for a trip  to mars in the 1950s in our timeline in  an interview with ew the show's creators  mentioned a friendly competition between  danny and ed to see who might get to  command the mission to mars it makes  sense then to open the trailer with  these two characters  and based on what we see danny wins that  as mentioned we do see her on the  mission and on this one shot you can see  that she's wearing the mission badge  nasa's ship is called the sojourner one  there's a shot of it approaching the red  planet and i'm guessing this first shot  is also it taking off from the surface  of the moon we also get a look at the  soviet ship during its terrestrial  launch it's called mars 94 which is  taken from an actual proposal that they  made to visit mars in 1994 but of course  in our timeline the soviet union had  been dissolved by that year as has  become standard for this show we don't  see much from the soviet perspective in  this trailer it's interesting that in  the alternate timeline there are still  two competing super powers we did find  out in the opening montage of season two  that they avoided getting bogged down  fighting in afghanistan and it's  possible the chernobyl disaster was  averted in the same way as we know the  three-mile island was in this timeline  remember the catalyst for the show is  that the soviets beat the us to land the  first man on the moon because of that  the space race continued and you see  several indications in this trailer that  nasa is determined to get to mars first  and get a win in one shot you see the  now short-haired margot addressing her  staff in a meeting saying we're not  going to come in second place again to  anyone that last part hints at the third  party that's entered the race in the  years that have passed since season two  my assumption is this large ship in  orbit above earth was built by a private  company called helios aerospace you see  their ceo dev isa on tv talking about  disagreeing with the idea that private  citizens don't belong in space their  ship is called phoenix and my guess is  that ed left nasa after losing the  competition to command sojourner and is  now in charge of helios's mission it  also looks like kelly has followed in  her father's footsteps you see her on a  ship or maybe in a base saying we're  talking about discovering life on  another planet it will change our  concept of who we are where we're going  there's another shot with ed and it  looks like she's saying this to him and  the reason why i thought it might be on  the surface is that you see a russian  suit hanging behind him  the helios suits appear to be blue and  there are some shots of them on mars in  one they're unloading what almost looks  like a rover but the markings say hab1  perhaps that is what they're in in the  previous shots and it can be moved  around or at least unloaded on wheels  you hear the helios ceo say that being  first is what it's all about with what  margot said earlier it looks like both  sides could be in a position to push  things and if ed is the commander of  phoenix then it makes sense that he  would be pushing since he knows what  it's like to miss out on the opportunity  to be first from way back on apollo 10  when he followed his mission instead of  touching down on the moon and being the  first person to do so this could be his  chance to erase that what if memory it  looks like things will go wrong when  they get there you hear that massive  dust storms have obscured both landing  sites this makes it sound like it comes  down to helios and nasa if there are  only two but there are these other shots  of cosmonauts preparing as well we know  they will get there there are several  shots of landers and plenty of activity  on the surface so the drama will be and  who is the first to land i guess also  finding the water seems to be an issue  at first at least you hear the ceo  asking where it is  later ed is talking to kelly about a  resource that can support large-scale  human colonization it's not clear from  the trailer what he's talking about and  i'm no expert here but a google search  will tell you that there are ample  resources that could be useful for  colonization available on mars so much  so that it seems like most strategies to  set up a permanent settlement would  involve sending automated ships ahead of  any human missions to get things set up  ahead of time not sure if they already  did that or if that will have anything  to do with their conversation but i did  go down a rabbit hole reading about it  so i thought i would mention it part of  what's interesting about ed working for  the private firm is that they may be  actively poaching people from nasa we do  have several shots of mission control  where it looks like bill aka peanut has  finally made it to flight director and  it's possible that alita will as well  because she's in that same position we  see margot molly and even ellen at jsc  so i don't know who that leaves to be on  ed's side over at helios there's a shot  of molly with a white cane so i'm  guessing she's blind now but it doesn't  appear to be holding her back from  working at nasa there is a shot of  helios mission control and i don't  notice any familiar faces there's a shot  of karen that might be there and her  going into private space travel with sam  was a popular theory but she could also  be there because of ed and kelly since  we don't know anything about where deb  iesa came from it's hard to put things  together in that part of the story there  are a lot of unknowns danny appears to  be an astronaut now too and in this one  shot of him that looks like it's at jsc  you can't miss that he has a wedding  ring on i looked at the cast list on  imdb and noticed an amber stevens who i  suppose is his wife and i guess that  means nine years later he's moved on  from his obsession with karen after her  midlife crisis situation that happened  there at the end of season two  whether the baldwin stayed together will  be one of the answers we'll get in  season three i don't see anything in  this trailer that would indicate if they  did one way or the other what looks like  one of the big space sequences we'll get  early in the season is some kind of an  issue on the phoenix while it's still in  earth's orbit there's a cable that's  broken loose and two astronauts in grey  suits getting knocked off the ring  originally i thought this was during  construction but there's this shot of  the interior where you see people  falling over that's probably related to  that i don't really know there are  several shots of civilians walking  around in the ring section and none of  anything that looks like a journey to  mars  so maybe helios has built this and is  showing it off before sending it to the  red planet a couple of shots that are  probably related to this accident have  an astronaut in a similar gray suit  hanging near a thruster and opening a  panel there's another one that has what  i guess is the same cable still whipping  around and this almost looks like danny  to me that doesn't seem right since he  was at nasa so i guess we'll have to  wait and see what's going on here it  does look like there'll be plenty of  action there are quite a few shots of  things looking hectic in space and the  last big thing that stands out is that  it looks like ellen has moved into  politics there's a shot of her running  for senate in 86 and i guess it must be  a flashback or part of the opening  montage if they do that again and with  the confetti falling from above it looks  like she probably won her race this  could be interesting considering there  would be presidential elections in 1992  and 96. if the season opens in 92 and  they get to mars in 95 then president  ellen wilson might happen this season it  all looks pretty exciting you see signs  that technology continues to outpace our  timeline there are flat screen displays  everywhere i'm curious to see how some  of those final notes of season two  affected things in the time between that  we didn't see and i think that's a good  place to leave things let me know in the  comments what you think about this  trailer what i missed and what you  thought i got right and what i got wrong  and what you're hoping to see please  like this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

